<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3. Frontend Technology Stack &amp; Client Architecture</h2>

The frontend is built with <strong>React 19</strong> using <strong>TypeScript</strong> for end-to-end type safety, compiled via <strong>Vite 6</strong> into an ultra-lean static distribution.

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.1 Technology Composition</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>React 19 (Hooks &amp; Concurrent Mode):</strong> Manages interactive UI states, including real-time visual floor plans, modal security gates, and audit dashboards.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Tailwind CSS v4:</strong> Modern styling system utilizing <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">@import "tailwindcss";</code> without external CSS bundle bloat.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Framer Motion (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">motion</code>):</strong> Smooth, hardware-accelerated transitions across module switches, status banner alerts, and dialog modals.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Lucide React:</strong> High-clarity iconography representing asset classes, security statuses, and hardware ports.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>html5-qrcode:</strong> High-speed camera barcode scanner decoding Code-128, Code-39, and QR code formats directly from device video streams at 30 fps.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Native HID Keyboard Event Listeners:</strong> Direct capture of physical USB barcode laser guns (Honeywell/Zebra/Symbol) operating in keyboard emulation mode.</li>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.2 Modular Component Structure</h3>
<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">
src/
├── components/
│   ├── InteractiveFloorMap.tsx     # 7th Floor Work Bay Grid &amp; Switch Port Allocation
│   ├── ScannerGate.tsx             # Dual-Mode Camera &amp; USB Laser Barcode Clearance Terminal
│   ├── ManagerChatbot.tsx          # Executive AI Assistant (Exclusive to Module B)
│   ├── AuditLogViewer.tsx          # Master Compliance Audit Log &amp; Filter Table
│   └── ScrapBacktrackModal.tsx     # Reversible Custody &amp; Scrap Decommission Terminal
├── services/
│   └── api.ts                      # Centralized Typed API Client (Axios/Fetch with retry logic)
├── utils/
│   ├── serialValidator.ts          # Barcode prefix stripping &amp; uppercase normalization
│   └── exportUtils.ts              # CSV &amp; Excel compliance report generation
├── types/
│   └── index.ts                    # Global TypeScript interfaces (Asset, Ticket, AuditEvent)
└── App.tsx                         # Core Application Router, RBAC Gate &amp; Shell
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.3 Hardware Barcode &amp; Input Normalization Engine</h3>
When barcode scanners scan serial labels, they often introduce scanner-specific metadata, prefixes (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">S/N:</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">CPU-</code>), or newline characters (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">\r\n</code>). The system implements a client-side sanitization layer:

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">typescript
/<em></em>
 * Normalizes input from both optical camera readers and physical USB laser scanners.
 * Strips hardware vendor prefixes, whitespace, and non-printable control characters.
 */
export function sanitizeBarcode(rawInput: string): string {
  if (!rawInput) return '';
  return rawInput
    .trim()
    .toUpperCase()
    .replace(/^(S\/N|SN|SERIAL|TAG|ASSET)[:\-_\s]*/i, '') // Strips vendor prefixes
    .replace(/[\x00-\x1F\x7F]/g, '');                   // Strips ASCII control bytes
}
</pre>

