<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">4.2 High-Throughput Gate Clearance Engine</h3>
The <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">/api/gate/verify</code> controller is designed for sub-5 millisecond response times at physical security gates:

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">typescript
// Pseudocode Logic for /api/gate/verify
app.post('/api/gate/verify', async (req, res) =&gt; {
  const { barcode, officerId } = req.body;
  const cleanSerial = sanitizeBarcode(barcode);

  // 1. Resolve asset from in-memory cache
  const asset = db.assets.find(a =&gt; a.serialNumber === cleanSerial);
  if (!asset) {
    recordAuditSecurityBreach({ cleanSerial, officerId, reason: 'UNREGISTERED_HARDWARE' });
    return res.status(403).json({ status: 'BLOCKED', message: 'Asset not found in database' });
  }

  // 2. Resolve active movement ticket
  const ticket = db.tickets.find(t =&gt; t.assetId === asset.id &amp;&amp; t.status === 'APPROVED');
  if (!ticket) {
    recordAuditSecurityBreach({ cleanSerial, officerId, reason: 'NO_APPROVED_TICKET' });
    return res.status(403).json({ status: 'BLOCKED', message: 'No APPROVED ticket found for this asset' });
  }

  // 3. Mark ticket and asset cleared
  ticket.status = 'CLEARED';
  ticket.clearedAt = new Date().toISOString();
  ticket.clearedByOfficer = officerId;
  asset.custodyState = 'TRANSIT_CLEARED';

  // 4. Trigger atomic file persistence
  await persistDatabase();

  return res.json({ status: 'CLEARED', asset, ticket });
});
</pre>

---

<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5. Reverse Proxy Architecture: Nginx with SSL/TLS</h2>

To meet enterprise compliance requirements, <strong>Nginx</strong> serves as the Layer-7 reverse proxy on Rocky Linux 9, handling SSL/TLS termination, HTTP-to-HTTPS redirection, and reverse-proxy buffering.

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:16px 0; font-size:10pt; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">
  <tr style="background-color:#0f3b7a; color:#ffffff;">
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">NGINX INGRESS CONFIGURATION</th>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">[ Client: TCP 80 (HTTP) ]   ──► HTTP 301 Redirect ──► [ Client: TCP 443 ]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">[ Client: TCP 443 (HTTPS) ] ──► SSL Termination   ──► [ Upstream Proxy ]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">(TLS 1.2 / TLS 1.3)   Passes to 127.0.0.1:3000</td>
  </tr>
</table>

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5.1 Production Nginx Virtual Host Specification</h3>
File path: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">/etc/nginx/conf.d/asset-tracker.conf</code>

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">nginx
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">==============================================================================</h1>
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">[24]7.ai Asset Tracker - Nginx Reverse Proxy Configuration</h1>
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">==============================================================================</h1>

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">1. Plain HTTP (Port 80) -&gt; Force Redirect to HTTPS (Port 443)</h1>
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name _;

    # Immediate 301 Permanent Redirect
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">2. Secure HTTPS (Port 443) -&gt; Reverse Proxy to Node.js (Port 3000)</h1>
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name _;

    # SSL Certificate Paths
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/asset-tracker.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/asset-tracker.key;

    # SSL Protocols &amp; Ciphers (Mozilla Modern Standard)
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    ssl_ciphers ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384;
    ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;
    ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;
    ssl_session_timeout 1d;
    ssl_session_tickets off;

    # Enterprise Security Headers
    add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
    add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;

    # Maximum payload size for audit exports and batch inventory syncs
    client_max_body_size 50M;

    # Reverse Proxy Location Routing
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;

        # WebSocket &amp; Upstream Connection Headers
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        
        # Real IP &amp; Forwarded Headers for Audit Logging
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;

        # Proxy Timeout Safeguards
        proxy_connect_timeout 60s;
        proxy_send_timeout 60s;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s;
        proxy_buffering off;
    }

    # Static Asset Caching Policy
    location ~* \.(js|css|png|jpg|jpeg|gif|ico|svg|woff|woff2)$ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        expires 30d;
        add_header Cache-Control "public, no-transform";
    }
}
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5.2 Operating System Hardening &amp; SELinux Policy</h3>
Under Rocky Linux 9, SELinux prevents Nginx from binding to upstream network sockets by default. The following commands configure the system:

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">bash
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">Allow Nginx reverse proxy connections through SELinux</h1>
setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect 1

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">Open standard HTTP (80) and HTTPS (443) services in firewalld</h1>
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=https
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=http
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-port=443/tcp
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-port=80/tcp
firewall-cmd --reload
</pre>

